# Rank 1242 / CVE-2023-51774: JSON::JWT.decode is the single public entry point
# of the json-jwt gem, and JSON::JWT.decode_compact_serialized picked the branch
# from the token itself -- `case jwt_string.count('.') + 1`, three segments to
# JWS.decode_compact_serialized and five to JWE.decode_compact_serialized. A
# caller that asked for a signed token therefore also accepted an encrypted one.
# Encrypting to a public key proves no identity, so anyone holding the recipient
# public key can mint a token whose claims the application reads as verified,
# and no signature is ever checked (CWE-347, sign/encryption confusion). The
# published proof of concept signs {"user":"admin"} as RS256, repackages the same
# claims as an RSA1_5 JWE, and both decode.
#
# Fix 9c4d842a94 ("reject blank JWE", the only change in v1.16.6) puts the
# encrypted branch behind a guard instead of entering it unconditionally:
#
#   when JWE::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
#     if allow_blank_payload
#       raise InvalidFormat.new("JWE w/ blank payload is not supported.")
#     else
#       JWE.decode_compact_serialized jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms, encryption_methods
#     end
#
# No flag on the pool row, and the commit is the real fix rather than a release
# bump: it is the sole non-version commit between v1.16.5 and v1.16.6, it touches
# only lib/json/jwt.rb, and v1.16.6 is the version the advisory records as fixed.
#
# FIXED. The weakness has no taint path and no misused API -- the token is a
# parameter of a library entry point and every call in the function is the
# library's own decoder -- so what has to be stated is the dispatch shape. The
# new Ruby extractor fact jose_compact_decode_accepts_encrypted_serialization
# holds when one function counts the compact-serialization separators of a
# token, reaches both a JWS decoder and a JWE decoder, and enters the encrypted
# branch with no guard on the line that follows the branch selector. The
# existing concept code.JwtUnverified and rule VYQL-CFG-005 judge it, because
# what the caller gets on that branch is a token whose signature was never
# verified; no new concept or rule is minted.
#
# The three clauses are what keep it off ordinary code. Counting '.' in a token
# is what a compact-serialization dispatcher does and almost nothing else does;
# requiring both a JWS decoder and a JWE decoder in the same function excludes
# every library that exposes the two serializations as separate entry points,
# which is the design RFC 7515 and RFC 7516 lead to; and the guard clause is the
# control -- a branch that raises, returns, or tests what the caller expected
# before decrypting is stating the serialization instead of inferring it.
#
# Measured bounded (timeout 180, --max-ram 4GB, --cache off): json-jwt at
# 9c4d842a94^ goes from 6 findings to 7, the extra one being VYQL-CFG-005 at
# lib/json/jwt.rb, and at 9c4d842a94 reports 6 with no VYQL-CFG-005. The gem's
# own spec tree, which calls JSON::JWT.decode on both serializations, reports
# none of them. ruby-jwt, jwe and rack-oauth2 report no VYQL-CFG-005 either.

test "rank1242: a compact JOSE decoder routes an encrypted token down the same entry point as a signed one"
  lang ruby
  file lib/json/jwt.rb
  expect VYQL-CFG-005
  code
  ```
  module JSON
    class JWT < ActiveSupport::HashWithIndifferentAccess
      class InvalidFormat < StandardError; end

      class << self
        def decode_compact_serialized(jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms = nil, encryption_methods = nil, allow_blank_payload = false)
          case jwt_string.count('.') + 1
          when JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            JWS.decode_compact_serialized jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms, allow_blank_payload
          when JWE::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            JWE.decode_compact_serialized jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms, encryption_methods
          else
            raise InvalidFormat.new("Invalid JWT Format. JWT should include #{JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS} or #{JWE::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS} segments.")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1242: the fix guards the encrypted branch before decrypting"
  lang ruby
  file lib/json/jwt.rb
  reject VYQL-CFG-005
  code
  ```
  module JSON
    class JWT < ActiveSupport::HashWithIndifferentAccess
      class InvalidFormat < StandardError; end

      class << self
        def decode_compact_serialized(jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms = nil, encryption_methods = nil, allow_blank_payload = false)
          case jwt_string.count('.') + 1
          when JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            JWS.decode_compact_serialized jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms, allow_blank_payload
          when JWE::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            if allow_blank_payload
              raise InvalidFormat.new("JWE w/ blank payload is not supported.")
            else
              JWE.decode_compact_serialized jwt_string, key_or_secret, algorithms, encryption_methods
            end
          else
            raise InvalidFormat.new("Invalid JWT Format. JWT should include #{JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS} or #{JWE::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS} segments.")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1242: an entry point that only accepts the signed serialization is not reported"
  lang ruby
  file lib/token/reader.rb
  reject VYQL-CFG-005
  code
  ```
  module Token
    class Reader
      class InvalidFormat < StandardError; end

      class << self
        def decode_compact_serialized(token, public_key, algorithms = nil)
          unless token.count('.') + 1 == JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            raise InvalidFormat.new("Expected a signed token of #{JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS} segments.")
          end
          JWS.decode_compact_serialized token, public_key, algorithms
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```

test "rank1242: a dispatcher that refuses the encrypted form unless the caller asked for it is not reported"
  lang ruby
  file lib/token/dispatcher.rb
  reject VYQL-CFG-005
  code
  ```
  module Token
    class Dispatcher
      class InvalidFormat < StandardError; end

      class << self
        def decode_compact_serialized(token, key, algorithms = nil, expect_encrypted = false)
          case token.count('.') + 1
          when JWS::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            JWS.decode_compact_serialized token, key, algorithms
          when JWE::NUM_OF_SEGMENTS
            raise InvalidFormat.new("An encrypted token is not accepted on this route.") unless expect_encrypted
            JWE.decode_compact_serialized token, key, algorithms
          else
            raise InvalidFormat.new("Unexpected number of segments.")
          end
        end
      end
    end
  end
  ```
